Subject: [PATCH] Propagate native Lua errors through the C++ exception wrapper

Local patch; not submitted upstream. With external unwinding, LuaJIT raises
Lua errors as foreign exceptions. They must reach lua_pcall; the catch-all
currently calls terminate without an active C++ exception. Rethrow after the
existing typed conversion handlers, preserving Lua error objects.

See https://luajit.org/extensions.html#exceptions for the interoperability
contract. Add regression cases for native Lua errors, object identity,
existing exception conversions, and successful calls. Loader regressions
also cover the companion upstream BOM backport and the bundled Unicode
module whose BOM triggers the observed arm64 startup failure.

diff --git a/libaegisub/lua/utils.cpp b/libaegisub/lua/utils.cpp
--- a/libaegisub/lua/utils.cpp
+++ b/libaegisub/lua/utils.cpp
@@ -230,7 +230,9 @@
 		return lua_error(L);
 	}
 	catch (...) {
-		std::terminate();
+		// LuaJIT can unwind Lua errors through C++ frames. Let lua_pcall
+		// handle them without replacing the error object or aborting.
+		throw;
 	}
 }
 
